2-3|Clue or Gear: The party finds a helpful clue or piece of gear ([[d100]] on the Pilfer Pouch UF table p.48).
4|Lore: The party learns a new piece of lore through a ceiling fresco, wall tapestry, bas-relief, old scroll, artefact, and so on. At the GM’s option, a player might introduce new lore relevant to their PC instead (if so, +2 xp).
5|Resource: A party resource is somehow used up, damaged, lost, left behind, or otherwise expended. Roll for which PC and a random piece of Pack Gear.
6-8|A Random Encounter occurs.
9|Warning sign of nearby danger (prints, scratches, nest materials, sounds, scents, droppings, remains of recent victim, etc).
10|Terrain change (visibility, temperature, water, odour, stability/footing, etc).
11-12|Potential Ally: The PCs find a prisoner, opposing faction, enemy turncoat, third party, other adventurers, etc.